"gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-01-07T14:21:09Z","label":{"name":"orm","color":"20C0B0"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":5858101302,"node_id":"MIE_lADOCX5JB85BWBK9zwAAAAFdK4g2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/5858101302","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"milestoned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-01-07T14:21:15Z","milestone":{"title":"1.4.x"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1007454510","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7545#issuecomment-1007454510","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7545","id":1007454510,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB848DIku","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-01-07T14:35:54Z","updated_at":"2022-01-07T14:37:07Z","body":"the mapper assumes objects of type \"B\" cannot be loaded polymorphically because it has no polymorphic_identity.  so it sets the identity keys for B objects (which includes C) to look like (B, [<id>]).  this produces a mismatch with use_get in this case, since you have D->A, it's looking for an identity key of (A, [<id>]).\r\n\r\none way the mapper can fix your case, is to just make the identity key for all non-concrete mapped classes based on the basemost class, regardless of polymorphic_identity being available.  but this breaks some assumptions that are made for class hierarchies that don't have polymorphic_identity attributes set up.   revisiting those assumptions is probably an option, but not in 1.4.30, and probably not at all because it's much easier to emit a warning here so that you can change your mapping to make the intent clear.\r\n\r\nThe warning is:\r\n\r\n\"Mapper Mapper[B(a)] does not indicate a polymorphic_identity, yet is part of an inheritance hierarchy that has a polymorphic_on column of 'a.type'.  Objects of this type cannot be loaded polymorphically which can lead to degraded or incorrect loading behavior in some scenarios.  Please establish a polmorphic_identity for this class, or leave it un-mapped.  To omit mapping an intermediary class when using declarative, set the `'__abstract__ = True'` attribute on that class.\"\r\n\r\n\r\nin your test case, it looks a lot like you don't want B mapped by itself, you would never instantiate a B() object.  So make it abstract:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nclass B(A):\r\n    __abstract__ = True\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1007454510/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1007455082","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7545#issuecomment-1007455082","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7545","id":1007455082,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB848DItq","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-01-07T14:36:32Z","updated_at":"2022-01-07T14:36:32Z","body":"patch for the warning\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/mapper.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/mapper.py\r\nindex dbcbc8a1b7..087a64eef9 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/mapper.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/mapper.py\r\n@@ -1044,6 +1044,23 @@ class Mapper(\r\n             if self.polymorphic_identity is not None and not self.concrete:\r\n                 self._identity_class = self.inherits._identity_class\r\n             else:\r\n+                if (\r\n+                    self.inherits\r\n+                    and self.inherits.base_mapper.polymorphic_on is not None\r\n+                ):\r\n+                    util.warn(\r\n+                        \"Mapper %s does not indicate a polymorphic_identity, \"\r\n+                        \"yet is part of an inheritance hierarchy that has a \"\r\n+                        \"polymorphic_on column of '%s'.  Objects of this type \"\r\n+                        \"cannot be loaded polymorphically which can lead to \"\r\n+                        \"degraded or incorrect loading behavior in some \"\r\n+                        \"scenarios.  Please establish a polmorphic_identity \"\r\n+                        \"for this class, or leave it un-mapped.  \"\r\n+                        \"To omit mapping an intermediary class when using \"\r\n+                        \"declarative, set the '__abstract__ = True' \"\r\n+                        \"attribute on that class.\"\r\n+                        % (self, self.inherits.base_mapper.polymorphic_on)\r\n+                    )\r\n                 self._identity_class = self.class_\r\n \r\n             if self.version_id_col is None:\r\ndiff --git a/test/orm/inheritance/test_basic.py b/test/orm/inheritance/test_basic.py\r\nindex 5fc69bf9ee..ab01d703db 100644\r\n--- a/test/orm/inheritance/test_basic.py\r\n+++ b/test/orm/inheritance/test_basic.py\r\n@@ -35,6 +35,10 @@ from sqlalchemy.testing import eq_\r\n from sqlalchemy.testing import fixtures\r\n from sqlalchemy.testing import is_\r\n from sqlalchemy.testing import mock\r\n+from sqlalchemy.testing.assertions import (\r\n+    expect_raises_message,\r\n+    expect_warnings,\r\n+)\r\n from sqlalchemy.testing.assertsql import AllOf\r\n from sqlalchemy.testing.assertsql import CompiledSQL\r\n from sqlalchemy.testing.assertsql import Conditional\r\n@@ -3501,7 +3505,12 @@ class NoPolyIdentInMiddleTest(fixtures.MappedTest):\r\n         cls.mapper_registry.map_imperatively(\r\n             A, base, polymorphic_on=base.c.type\r\n         )\r\n-        cls.mapper_registry.map_imperatively(B, inherits=A)\r\n+\r\n+        with expect_warnings(\r\n+            r\"Mapper Mapper\\[B\\(base\\)\\] does not indicate a \"\r\n+            \"polymorphic_identity,\"\r\n+        ):\r\n+            cls.mapper_registry.map_imperatively(B, inherits=A)\r\n         cls.mapper_registry.map_imperatively(\r\n             C, inherits=B, polymorphic_identity=\"c\"\r\n         )\r\n@@ -3511,6 +3520,7 @@ class NoPolyIdentInMiddleTest(fixtures.MappedTest):\r\n         cls.mapper_registry.map_imperatively(\r\n             E, inherits=A, polymorphic_identity=\"e\"\r\n         )\r\n+        cls.mapper_registry.configure()\r\n \r\n     def test_load_from_middle(self):\r\n         C, B = self.classes.C, self.classes.B\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1007455082/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":f